You are correct.  Once an item enters a game, it will not be regenerated in
*any* other situation.  Even if destroyed!

Greg.  I can think of four likely places (right off) that your game's
Stormbringer can be.

1.	The weapons room in the castle.
	In previous games I have played I have found a named weapon in this
	room.  Sunsword I do believe.  You must check this room to be sure.
	Since a lot of weapons are generated to create this room, it is possible
	for named weapons to show up here.  Kinda like shops.

2.	Priest in a temple has it.
	Turns out that there is a chance for temple priest to get *artifacts*.
	This (when I learned of the code) I thought to be a major pain,
	because of just this situation.  If you want your Stormbringer, you
	may have to kill your own priest to get it!

3.	Ghost level.
	If you have (unknowingly) passed up a bones level of a character who
	owned a Strombringer, you have passed up your only chance for the item.

4.	Any unkilled monster could be carrying it.
	If you did not kill every monster (a virtually impossible task) before
	you were "blessed" with your broadsword, a random monster could be
	carrying it.  The chances for this are *remote* but possible.

	I once killed a sewer rat and found an Axe named Cleaver.

The chances of any of this happening in any game are terribly small, however
it looks like you just got "lucky" in your best game ever.

Keep looking Greg.  You'll find it.

